The '''night beast''' is a [[superior]] variant of the [[dark beast]]. It has a chance of spawning after purchasing the unlock ''Bigger and Badder'' for 50 [[Slayer reward point]]s from any [[Slayer master|Slayer Master]]. Unlike their normal variants, a night beast's initial attack is always magic, regardless if the player hits it first or if it made to aggro with a [[goading potion]]. It will always attempt to melee the player unless they cannot reach them, in which they will begin using magic until this no longer occurs.

The night beast has a special attack where it will briefly stop attacking then it uses Magic for three attacks which resemble [[Fire Blast]], covering a 3x3 area dealing damage  equal to 1/3 of the player's current [[Hitpoints]] (rounded down). If the player is below 3 hitpoints the special attack's damage will round down to 0 so it is incapable of killing you{{CiteDiscord|author=Mod Ash|url=https://discord.com/channels/324132423636090880/431834766325841920/1416025128088899676|date=12 September 2025|quote=Looks to me like the spec really is calculating your current HP / 3, which would round down to zero as you say. The standard magic attack can hit up to 8, though, and it'd do that more often than the spec, so caution is advised.|image=Night_beast_spec.png|ctximage=CiteDiscord - night beast spec question.png|ctxquote= would you be able to confirm exactly how the night beast's (superior dark beast) magic attack damage works? The wiki says 1/3 hp rounded down, and various people and my own experience suggest that at low enough hp this damage always rounds down to 0 meaning you never die from it (assuming you're praying against its melee attacks). Rounding down to 0 was previously on the wiki but it was removed with the claim that it can kill you so I was looking for official word on how its damage works |notes=|name=|group=|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/27962833#chat-messages-431834766325841920-1416025128088899676|archivedate=8 March 2026}} (note that this rounding '''does not''' apply to the standard magic attack the night beast will do when first attacked by the player or when the player is out of melee range). The simplest strategy is to use the protection from melee prayer and let the special attacks hit you, making sure you do not leave the monster's melee range. 

[[File:Night beast AoE attack.png|thumb|right|250px|A player is hit by the night beast's area-of-effect attack.]]

==Drops==
''In addition to 100% drops and tertiary drops, superior Slayer monsters will always roll 3 additional items, of which only 1 roll may be from the superior unique table. The other rolls are performed on the regular counterpart's table; their displayed drop chances represent a single roll.''

{{DropLogProject|kills=47056}}

{{AverageSuperiorDrop|90|mobname=night beast}} In the [[Iorwerth Dungeon]], the average kill (excluding the superior unique table) is instead worth {{Coins|{{#expr:{{Average drop value|raw=y}} + 2.5 * 8 * ({{GEP|Divine super combat potion(4)}} - {{GEP|Super combat potion(4)}}) - {{GEP|Mist battlestaff|1 / 73}} - {{GEP|Dust battlestaff|1 / 73}} - {{GEP|Eternal gem |1 / 256}} - {{GEP|Imbued heart|1 / 256}} round 0}}}} due to the guaranteed drop of 6 to 10 [[crystal shard]]s. This value for crystal shards assumes that they are made into [[Divine super combat potion|divine super combat potions]].

